      "narration_text": "On July 14, 2026, IBM released selected preliminary second-quarter results ahead of its earnings call. The market reaction was brutal: shares fell about twenty-five percent. Yet the official numbers were not a collapse. Revenue was seventeen point two billion dollars, up one percent. Software rose five percent, consulting was flat, and infrastructure fell seven percent. Operating earnings were two dollars and ninety-three cents per share, up five percent from a year earlier."
