      "narration_text": "The deeper problem was what IBM said happened in June. Clients redirected quarterly capital spending toward servers, storage, and memory to secure constrained infrastructure before expected price increases. IBM said it expected some supply-chain impact, but not the scale of the reprioritization. Then came the admission: the company faltered, moved too slowly, and large deals failed to close on schedule."
